Verse 1:
[Db]Beneath the cross of Jesus I [Ab7/Gb]fain [Fm]would [Ebm]take [Ab7]mystand,
[Cdim]The [Bbm]shadow of [Cdim]amightyrock [Bbm/F]within [Gb]a weary [Fm]land;
[Db]A home within the wilderness, a [Gb]rest upon [Bbm]the [Ebm]way,
[Ebm]From the [Ab7]burning of the [Db]noontide heat, [Gb]and the [Db/Ab]burden [Fm/Ab]of [Ab7]the [Db]day.

Verse 2:
[Db]Upon that cross of [Fm]Jesus
[Db]mine eye at times [Fm]can [Ab7]see
[Cdim]the [Bbm]very [Bb7/D]dying [Bbm/F]form [Gb]of One
[Cdim]who [Bbm]suffered [Ebm]there [Gb]for me;
[Db]and from my stricken heart [Gb]with [Bbm]tears
[Db]two wonders I [Gb]confess:
[Ebm]the [Ab7]wonders [Db]of redeeming [Ab7]love
[Ebm]and [Ab7]my unworthiness.

Verse 3:
[Db]I take, O cross, thy [Fm]shadow
[Db]for my abiding [Ebm]place;
[Cdim]I [Bbm]ask no other sunshine [Gb]than
[Cdim]the [Bbm]sunshine [Ebm]of [Gb]his face;
[Db]content to let the world [Gb]go [Bbm]by,
[Db]to know no gain [Gb]nor [Bbm/F]loss,
[Ebm]my [Ab7]sinful [Db]self my [Gb]only [Ab7]shame,
[Ebm]my [Ab7]glory [Db/F]all [Gb]the [Fm/Ab]cross.
